Dock cards' moves get a per-window animation config (updateDockMoveAnimation) whose
curve overshoots by decoration:keystone_bounce * keystone_bounce_decay^depth, the
depth from a `dockd<N>` tag features/sidedock sets: a slide-in bounce damped card by
card, without switching the shared windowsMove curve under cards already moving
(Hyprland reads a curve live, so a shared one switched between cards bent those
already moving). The window owns the config; the animation holds it weakly.

